# Reviewed, accepted-risk findings only - per docs/adr/0010, HIGH/CRITICAL
# with no upstream fix get a justified entry here, not a loosened gate.
# Re-evaluate whenever cosign's pinned version (Dockerfile, currently
# v3.1.4 - verified as the actual latest release, not just assumed) or the
# base image changes: if either has since shipped a fix, remove the
# matching entry and let a rebuild resolve it instead.
#
# Last audit: a scan of this exact image with no ignore file at all, every
# entry below matched against its result. The move to cosign v3.1.4, the
# current python:3.12-slim and build-time Debian updates made eighteen
# earlier entries (cosign's Go dependencies, two openssl CVEs) stale - they
# were removed, not left in place to quietly widen the gate.

# --- base OS (python:3.12-slim) - same package family as, and same
# reasoning as, services/gateway/.trivyignore: base-OS packages in a code
# path this container (Python + a single cosign subprocess call, non-root,
# no mount/cgroup capabilities) never exercises.
CVE-2025-69720
CVE-2026-16742
CVE-2026-54369
CVE-2026-76642
CVE-2026-78408
CVE-2026-78409
CVE-2026-78410
CVE-2026-9538

# --- libsqlite3-0: FTS5 heap overflows (DoS / code execution on a crafted
# FTS5 index or prefix query) and a session-extension overflow in
# sqlite3changeset_apply(). Debian status "affected", no fix shipped. Checked
# in this image rather than assumed: verify.py imports only the standard
# library and never SQLite. filelock (pulled in by huggingface_hub) does
# ship an SQLite-backed ReadWriteLock, but loads sqlite3 lazily on first use
# of that class, nothing in the image references it, and its SQL uses
# neither FTS5 nor the session extension - the only code these CVEs live in.
CVE-2026-119373
CVE-2026-119374
CVE-2026-119379

# --- cosign v3.1.4 (latest release) still vendors golang.org/x/net v0.61.0:
# x/net/html quadratic-time parsing of crafted HTML (fixed in 0.62.0, in no
# cosign release yet). cosign here runs one `verify-blob` against a local
# bundle; at worst a hostile HTML response would stall this one-shot Job,
# which fails closed - vLLM never starts. Availability only, never integrity.
CVE-2026-78661
